SOAPBOX: Due to a wedding on the Saturday this was always going to be a
SOAPBOX: part time affair, so I decided that I would try assisted and
SOAPBOX: basically chase some DX. Of course after 2 weeks of perfect
SOAPBOX: weather it bucketed down rain from Saturday night through to
SOAPBOX: Monday morning and the TH6DXX (or BN86 Balun) filled with water
SOAPBOX: and presented a very bad VSWR on 10/15 and 20m. The spare dipoles
SOAPBOX: erected for this very scenario were not much assistance as gain
SOAPBOX: is needed from Oceania to work anyone. Unfortunately the fault
SOAPBOX: with the 40m rotatable dipole went from intermittent to
SOAPBOX: persistent so 40m was out as well. All considered I worked some
SOAPBOX: nice DX but could not be heard much of the time. Thank to the
SOAPBOX: guys in the Carribean and Atlantic for hearing me and finally
SOAPBOX: figuring out it was Victor Lima not Zulu Lima. Yes, I know the
SOAPBOX: accents are similar to most of you - vastly different to a kiwi
SOAPBOX: or Aussie ear. Scores from the big guns are amazing. Never tried
SOAPBOX: to run, nice to have at least a small opening to EU on 15m. D4D
SOAPBOX: heard long path but weak and could not be worked. Shame it is
SOAPBOX: probably an ATNO on 15m for me. Looking forward to the CW leg
SOAPBOX: and perhaps a new antenna on the tower by then. Regards Tony -
SOAPBOX: VL3E/VK3TZ/AD2DO
